<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul bourse to delist two firms from 3-way merger.</title>
<headline>Seoul bourse to delist two firms from 3-way merger.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Now Precision Co and Inkel Corp will be delisted from the Seoul stock market on Thursday after the two firms had been absorbed by Haitai Electronics Co, the Korea Stock Exchange said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Instead, Haitai will list 6.82 million new shares -- 5.63 million common and 1.19 million preferred shares.</p>
<p>The three-way merger took effect on November 1, the exchange said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
